gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.5218140184494002,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.0027951819369191333,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":47.2,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.2779670839945292,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.06138710673482691,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.72073,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Gyre Therapeutics, Inc., a pharmaceutical company, engages in the development and commercialization of small-molecule, anti-inflammatory, and anti-fibrotic drugs targeting organ fibrosis. The company offers ETUARY (Pirfenidone), an anti-fibrotic drug approved for the treatment of idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis; and under Phase 3 trials for the treatment of pneumoconiosis. It is also involved in the development of F351 (Hydronidone), a structural derivative of ETUARY under Phase 3 trials for the treatment of chronic hepatitis B (CHB)-associated liver fibrosis; and completed Phase 1 trials for the treatment of liver fibrosis associated with metabolic dysfunction-associated steatohepatitis. In addition, the company develops F573, which is in Phase 2 clinical trials for the treatment of acute/acute-on-chronic liver failure. Further, its preclinical products include F230 for the treatment of pulmonary arterial hypertension; and F528 to treat chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. Gyre Therapeutics, Inc. was founded in 2002 and is headquartered in San Diego, California. Gyre Therapeutics, Inc. operates as a subsidiary of GNI USA, Inc.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Ying  Luo Ph.D. | CEO, President & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $85,000 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 625 people. Revenue per employee of $187K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Gyre Therapeutics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $472M market cap on $117M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +151% over the past three years and +52% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -15% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 96% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $180,000 of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -9.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 72% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 10% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 293% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Gross margin tops the Healthcare peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Healthcare \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Comparing Hypermarcas (OTCMKTS:HYPMY) & Gyre Therapeutics (NASDAQ:GYRE)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/comparing-hypermarcas-otcmktshypmy-gyre-therapeutics-nasdaqgyre.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794388506.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Gyre Therapeutics (NASDAQ:GYRE) Releases Earnings Results, Beats Expectations By $0.19 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/gyre-therapeutics-nasdaqgyre-releases-earnings-results-beats-expectations-by-0-19-eps-2.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794104944.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Spru